<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Playwright on Ovaar - Software engineering blog</title><link>https://ovaar.github.io/tags/playwright/</link><description>Recent content in Playwright on Ovaar - Software engineering blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2020–2026 Thomas Reynders. Licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/</copyright><lastBuildDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://ovaar.github.io/tags/playwright/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>A robot that clicks around staging every night</title><link>https://ovaar.github.io/blog/nightly-seeded-random-walk-e2e/</link><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ovaar.github.io/blog/nightly-seeded-random-walk-e2e/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Our end-to-end tests follow scripts. Open the product, pick an option, go to the summary, check the price. They catch regressions in the paths we wrote down. They don&amp;rsquo;t catch the crash that only happens when you press Escape in a dialog, go Back, and click something else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So we added a test that doesn&amp;rsquo;t follow a script. Every night it opens our React product configurator on staging and clicks around at random for a few minutes, checking every screen it lands on. When it finds something, it prints a command that replays the exact same walk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On its second night it found a memory leak in our 3D viewer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="what-a-walk-does"&gt;What a walk does&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each walk starts from an entry page (home, the product list, the configurator) and repeats:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick an action, weighted: click, type or select on a visible control (80%), Tab (7%), Escape (7%), Shift+Tab (3%), browser Back (3%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wait for the app to settle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check the screen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ACTIONS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;control&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;weight&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;80&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;tab&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;weight&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;shift-tab&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;weight&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;escape&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;weight&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;back&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;weight&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;When it types into a field, it picks from a small list of inputs that hand-written tests rarely try:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;FILL_CORPUS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;a&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;x&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;repeat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Ünïcødé ✓ 日本語 🚀&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;bold&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;42&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;-1&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;0&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;1e9&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;3.14&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;After every step, it checks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no uncaught error and no &lt;code&gt;console.error&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no API response with status 500 or higher&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no raw translation key on screen (&lt;code&gt;summary.dialog.title&lt;/code&gt; instead of a label)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;NaN&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;[object Object]&lt;/code&gt; on screen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the page isn&amp;rsquo;t blank, has exactly one &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;main&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and at most one visible &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;h1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;focus doesn&amp;rsquo;t drop to &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; after Escape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Five walks run in a GitHub Actions workflow at 03:30, after the normal scripted suite. It never runs on pull requests and isn&amp;rsquo;t a required check. Its job is to find things, not to block merges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="same-seed-same-walk"&gt;Same seed, same walk&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A random test is only useful if you can reproduce what it found. All randomness comes from one seeded generator. It is &lt;a href="https://gist.github.com/tommyettinger/46a874533244883189143505d203312c"&gt;mulberry32&lt;/a&gt;, inline, because the walk needs nothing more than a 32-bit stream that replays the same way on every machine:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mulberry32&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Random&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mh"&gt;0x6d2b79f5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;imul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;imul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;61&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;14&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4294967296&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each run has one base seed (the CI run id, or &lt;code&gt;Date.now()&lt;/code&gt; locally). Each walk mixes in its own name with FNV-1a, so the five walks differ from each other but any one can be replayed on its own:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walkSeed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;base&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walk&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mh"&gt;0x811c9dc5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;char&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;base&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;char&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;codePointAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;imul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mh"&gt;0x01000193&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A failure names the rule, the step, the URL and the seed, and the job summary gets a command like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;E2E_EXPLORE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;E2E_SEED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;20261116&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;E2E_STEPS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;16&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; npx playwright &lt;span class="nb"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt; --project&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;explore-chromium --grep &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;walk from home&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;E2E_STEPS&lt;/code&gt; stops the replay at the failing step, so you land on the broken screen in Playwright&amp;rsquo;s UI mode instead of watching 400 steps go by.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One limit is worth stating: the seed fixes which actions the walk &lt;em&gt;chooses&lt;/em&gt;. It doesn&amp;rsquo;t fix what a shared staging backend returns or how long it takes. In practice the replay hits the same bug almost every time, but not always.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="it-must-not-break-staging"&gt;It must not break staging&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Staging is shared with the whole team. A robot that clicks every button would eventually request quotes, upload files and edit customer records. Steering it away from dangerous buttons isn&amp;rsquo;t enough, because buttons get renamed. So safety has two layers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steering.&lt;/strong&gt; The walk never touches file inputs, &lt;code&gt;type=submit&lt;/code&gt; buttons, download links, links that open a new tab, links that leave the app, or a short list of names like the &amp;ldquo;send request&amp;rdquo; button (in all nine languages, because the walk can switch language).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The guarantee is at the network layer.&lt;/strong&gt; Every request goes through &lt;code&gt;page.route&lt;/code&gt;, and every write to the API is aborted unless it is on an allow-list:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;blockReason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawUrl&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;READ_METHODS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;has&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;toUpperCase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isOurApi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hostname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;blocked&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BLOCKED_WRITES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;find&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pattern&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pattern&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pathname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;blocked&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;blocked&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;reason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;allowed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ALLOWED_WRITES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;some&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;methods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pattern&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;methods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;has&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pattern&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pathname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;allowed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;write to an endpoint the walk does not allow&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The allow-list is the draft-configuration endpoints, verb by verb, with real GUIDs for ids (so a path like &lt;code&gt;/configurator/pdf&lt;/code&gt; can&amp;rsquo;t pass as an id). Each entry also names its HTTP methods, so a stray &lt;code&gt;DELETE&lt;/code&gt; to a draft path is blocked too. Anything with &lt;code&gt;quot&lt;/code&gt; in the path is always blocked.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The important part is the last line. A new endpoint that writes data is blocked by default and shows up as a &lt;code&gt;blocked-request&lt;/code&gt; violation. &lt;strong&gt;It fails closed.&lt;/strong&gt; That is the opposite of what my first draft did, which was a list of endpoints to block.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The walk also stubs &lt;code&gt;window.print&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;window.open&lt;/code&gt;, and dismisses any stray browser dialog.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="settling-without-a-destination"&gt;Settling without a destination&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The usual Playwright advice is to wait for a specific element, never a fixed time. A random walk has no destination to wait for. And &lt;code&gt;networkidle&lt;/code&gt; doesn&amp;rsquo;t help in a single-page app: it resolves at once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So the walk tracks requests itself and waits until none have been in flight for 400 ms, capped at 5 seconds so a streaming 3D model can&amp;rsquo;t stall it:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;trackRequests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;Page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inFlight&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;Request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastChange&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;touch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastChange&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;request&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inFlight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;touch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;requestfinished&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inFlight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;touch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;requestfailed&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inFlight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;touch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;settle() {&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;until&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pause&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// let a request the last action triggered register
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;until&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;inFlight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;size&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastChange&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pause&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A screen that fails a check is read again 1.5 seconds later, and only violations that are still there count. Without that, every loading skeleton caught mid-transition would be a failure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="keeping-the-rules-honest"&gt;Keeping the rules honest&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rules live outside the browser.&lt;/strong&gt; Everything that &lt;em&gt;decides&lt;/em&gt; is a pure function with unit tests: the PRNG, the action filter, the network block, the screen rules, the allow-list matcher. The Playwright side only reads facts from the page and drives the walk. That makes the rules cheap to test and keeps flakes out of them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A walk that does nothing fails.&lt;/strong&gt; A walk of 10 or more steps that never clicked, filled or selected a control fails as &lt;code&gt;no-control-acted&lt;/code&gt;, instead of passing green because it spent five minutes pressing Tab on an error page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I checked that each rule can fail.&lt;/strong&gt; Before merging I put one violation of each kind into a real walk: an uncaught error, a &lt;code&gt;console.error&lt;/code&gt;, a 500, a blocked write, a raw key, &lt;code&gt;NaN&lt;/code&gt;, two &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;h1&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;s, a blank page, lost focus. All nine went red with the rule, step, URL, seed and replay command.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known bugs go on a narrow list.&lt;/strong&gt; Two things on &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; already failed the walk on day one. They went into a &lt;code&gt;KNOWN_VIOLATIONS&lt;/code&gt; list, each matched on its rule plus a narrow regex, with a reason. Entries only ever get removed:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DIALOG_OUTLIVES_ROUTE&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kt"&gt;KnownViolation&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rule&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;focus-lost&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Only a dialog that outlived its route: opened on one path, now on another.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;detail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/\(dialog opened on (\S+), now on (?!\1\))\S+\)$/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;reason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;dialog state sits above the routes, so a dialog stays open after browser Back; &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;closing it then has no trigger to return focus to&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The regex is the point. A dialog that loses focus on its &lt;em&gt;own&lt;/em&gt; route still fails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="what-it-found"&gt;What it found&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="a-webgl-viewer-that-never-died"&gt;A WebGL viewer that never died&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two nights in, a walk failed at step 484 with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;console-error: Rendering to a canvas that was resized to zero. If you see this message
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;you may be accidentally leaking a viewer instance. ErrorCode:14.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It was followed by dozens of &lt;code&gt;Cannot set properties of null (setting 'shareDepthFrom')&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our 3D view wraps Autodesk&amp;rsquo;s viewer. Leaving a 3D step while the viewer was still waiting for its auth token went like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React unmounted the component, and our hook removed the element.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The token arrived.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The wrapper built Autodesk&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;Viewer3D&lt;/code&gt; on the detached, zero-sized element and started its render loop. Nothing ever stopped it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Even without the error burst, every visit to a 3D step left one live viewer and one WebGL context behind. &lt;code&gt;window.NOP_VIEWERS.length&lt;/code&gt; went up by one per visit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A colleague added an idempotent &lt;code&gt;dispose()&lt;/code&gt; to the wrapper package, and the hook now calls it on every path that drops a viewer: unmount, both cancelled-init paths and the failed-init &lt;code&gt;catch&lt;/code&gt;. Each of the four cases has a test that fails on the old hook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No scripted test would have found this. You have to leave the page during a window of a few hundred milliseconds, on a slow network, and then keep going for a while.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="a-focus-check-that-raced-the-ui-library"&gt;A focus check that raced the UI library&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The walk also failed with &amp;ldquo;Escape dropped focus&amp;rdquo; on an image preview dialog. The failure snapshot showed focus &lt;em&gt;on the opener&lt;/em&gt;, so the app was right and the check was wrong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.radix-ui.com/"&gt;Radix&lt;/a&gt; returns focus in a &lt;code&gt;setTimeout(0)&lt;/code&gt; after the dialog unmounts, so between unmount and that timeout &lt;code&gt;document.activeElement&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. On a fast machine that gap is 5 ms. With 20x CPU throttling it&amp;rsquo;s 116 ms. The CI runner, busy rendering 3D, read focus right in that window.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The fix wasn&amp;rsquo;t to drop the rule. The check now reads focus every 50 ms and only reports a loss if focus is still on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; after 1.5 seconds. If focus is already on an element it reads once and doesn&amp;rsquo;t wait.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="smaller-things"&gt;Smaller things&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product on staging returned a 500 without CORS headers, so the browser could only report it as a CORS error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A link in the header with no accessible name.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dialog that stays open after browser Back (the known violation above).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="takeaways"&gt;Takeaways&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seed everything and print the replay command.&lt;/strong&gt; A random test without a replay is a flaky test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make safety fail closed.&lt;/strong&gt; Allow-list writes at the network layer, and treat a blocked write as a finding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the decisions in pure functions.&lt;/strong&gt; The browser side should only read and act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check every rule can fail before trusting it green.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expect to fix your own checks.&lt;/strong&gt; One of the first three failures was the test being wrong about timing. That&amp;rsquo;s fine, as long as the fix keeps the rule strict.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>